title: EMR Connect › Connect a system › Choose the system and contact
route: /emr
intro: The first two steps of the three-step 'Connect a system' pop-up: pick the kind of system and name it, then name the person at the practice who can approve read-only access.
dir: TD
also: The demo asks for no password, key or scope. Access is always read-only. In production the clinic provides a service account that lives in a credential vault and is never typed into the screen.
---
click s1 "Click 'Connect a system'\nPrimary button, top right of the page"
decision qp "Is Reader paused in Settings?"
toast tp "'Reader is paused'\n'Resume it in Settings to connect a system.'"
endx xp "Nothing opens"
overlay o1 "Connect a system\nRead-only. Nothing is written back until a person approves it.\nSteps: System, Contact, Test"

group gS1 "Step 1 of 3: System"
  input i1 "Pick one System type\nClinical record (default), Billing system, Practice management or Lab results"
  process p1 "Each choice shows what it holds\n'Charts, notes and medications', 'Claims and remittances', 'Schedules and admissions', 'Lab orders and results'"
  input i2 "Type a 'Name in Psyflo' (optional)\n'Shown in Connection health.'"
  input is "Choose the site the system serves\n'Site A', 'Site B' or 'Both sites' (starts at the sites in view)\nA one-site viewer sees 'It will serve Site B, the only site your role can see.' and no choice"
  process p2 "Blank name becomes '{kind} · Site A', '{kind} · Site B' or '{kind} · Both sites'"
  click c1 "Click 'Next'"
endgroup

group gS2 "Step 2 of 3: Contact"
  input i3 "Type 'Contact at the practice' (required)\nName and role, for example Dana Ruiz, practice manager"
  process p3 "'We email them a read-only access request. Until they approve it, the test below uses a demo record.'"
  ext x1 "Contact at the practice approves read-only access\nDemo: simulated, the test uses a demo record"
  click c2 "Click 'Run the connection test'"
  decision q1 "Is the contact filled in?"
  toast t1 "'Add the person at the practice who can approve read-only access.'\nClears when the person types"
  click c3 "Click 'Back'"
endgroup

click cx "Click 'Cancel' or the X, press Escape, or click the dimmed area\nOn any step"
endx e1 "Pop-up closes\nNothing is saved. Typed answers are lost"
goto g1 "Continues in: EMR Connect › Connect a system › Run the connection test and save"

s1 --> qp
qp -->|Yes| tp --> xp
qp -->|No| o1 --> i1
i1 --> p1 --> is --> i2 --> p2 --> c1
c1 --> i3
i3 --> p3
p3 -.-> x1
i3 --> c2 --> q1
q1 -->|No| t1 --> i3
q1 -->|Yes| g1
i3 -.-> c3
c3 -->|Choices are kept| i1
o1 -.-> cx
cx --> e1
